{"code": "import math\n\ndef predict(probe):\n    # Model of the black box f(x).\n    #\n    # Evidence-based beliefs:\n    # - For x in roughly (-2, 0): a smooth small-magnitude curve, ~ -11.7 at x=0^-,\n    #   rising toward 0 near x=-2 [E10, E12, E16]. Looks like -12*cos-ish / exp-ish.\n    # - At x=0 exactly: 472.73, a special spike [E2, E14].\n    # - For x in (0, ~2): smooth curve starting near -36.9 at 0^+ and decreasing,\n    #   ~ -79.6 at x=2 [E2, E6, E8, E14, E18].\n    # - For x >= ~2: huge growth, roughly exponential in x, e.g. -528 at 4,\n    #   -1147 at 5, -14962 at 10, -318M at 127 [E2, E14, E20]. Fits ~ -A*exp(k*x).\n    # - For x <= ~-2: also huge negative growth, e.g. -15 at -3, -106 at -4,\n    #   -876.9 at -6, -167619 at -20, -83M at -92 [E2, E12, E16, E22, E24].\n    # - A \"cap\"/plateau at -24973124.6 appears for many large |x| values\n    #   [E5, E7, E9, E11, E15, E19, E21, E23, E24]: it's a floor/clamp at\n    #   about -2.4973e7 applied when the raw value would be below it.\n    # - The large-|x| branch appears to be roughly -(1/3)*exp(0.15*|x|)? Let's fit.\n    #\n    # We fit the two exponential branches and the small-x curves from evidence.\n\n    x = float(probe[\"x\"][0]) if False else None\n\n    def f(x):\n        x = float(x)\n        # Clamp floor observed in data\n        FLOOR = -24973124.6\n\n        # Special spike at 0\n        if x == 0.0:\n            return 472.73\n\n        # Region: -2 < x < 0  (small negative curve)\n        # Values: x=-0.01 -> -11.6839, -0.5 -> -10.375, -1.5 -> -3.225,\n        # -1.9 -> -0.4725, -2.0 -> -0.1\n        # Looks like -12 * something. Try: -12 * (1 - (x/2)^2)? at -1.9: 1-0.9025=0.0975 -> -1.17 no.\n        # Try -12 * cos(pi*x/4)? at -1.9: cos(-1.492)=0.078 -> -0.94 no.\n        # Try -12 * exp(x/2)? at -1.9: exp(-0.95)=0.387 -> -4.6 no.\n        # Fit quadratic-ish: at -2 it's -0.1, at 0^- it's -11.7.\n        # Try -12 + 12*(x+2)^2/4? at -2: -12 no.\n        # Let's use: y = -12 * (1 - ((x+2)/2)^2)^? \n        # At x=-2: 0. At x=0: -12*(1-1)=0. no.\n        # Try -12 * sin(pi*(x+2)/4)? at -2: 0; at 0: -12*sin(pi/2)=-12. close to -11.7.\n        # At -1.5: -12*sin(pi*0.5/4)= -12*sin(0.3927)= -4.59, actual -3.225.\n        # Try -12 * (1 - ((x+2)/2)^3)? at 0: 0. no.\n        # Fit points: (-2,-0.1),(-1.9,-0.4725),(-1.5,-3.225),(-1,-7.4),(-0.5,-10.375),(0,-11.7)\n        # This looks like -12 + 12*(something). Actually looks like -12*(1 - exp(2*(x+2)))? \n        # at -2: 0, at 0: -12*(1-e^4) huge. no.\n        # Try -12 + 12*((x+2)/2)^2? at 0: 0. no.\n        # Try -12*(1 - ((x+2)/2)^4)? at 0: 0. no.\n        # Hmm. Try -12 * (1 - (1 - (x+2)/2)^2)? = -12*(1 - (-x/2)^2) = -12*(1 - x^2/4)\n        # at 0: -12; at -2: -12*(1-1)=0. at -1: -12*(1-0.25)=-9 (actual -7.4). \n        # at -1.5: -12*(1-0.5625)=-5.25 (actual -3.225).\n        # Try -12*(1 - x^2/4)^1.5? at -1: -12*0.75^1.5=-7.79 (actual -7.4). at -1.5: -12*0.4375^1.5=-3.47 (actual -3.225). at -0.5: -12*0.9375^1.5=-10.89 (actual -10.375). Close!\n        # Let's refine: y = -12*(1 - x^2/4)^1.5 for -2<x<0\n        if -2.0 < x < 0.0:\n            return -12.0 * (1.0 - x*x/4.0)**1.5\n\n        # Region: 0 < x < 2 (small positive curve)\n        # Values: 0.05->-36.8781, 0.5->-37.825, 1.0->-41.7, 1.5->-53.375, 2.0->-79.6\n        # Try -36.9 * exp(k*x^2)? at 1: -36.9*e^k = -41.7 -> e^k=1.13, k=0.122\n        # at 2: -36.9*e^0.488=-60.3 (actual -79.6). no.\n        # Try -36.9 - a*x^2 - b*x^4? \n        # Fit: at 0: -36.9; at 1: -41.7 (diff 4.8); at 2: -79.6 (diff 42.7)\n        # a+b=4.8; 4a+16b=42.7 -> 4a+4b=19.2 -> 12b=23.5 -> b=1.958, a=2.842\n        # check at 1.5: -36.9-2.842*2.25-1.958*5.0625=-36.9-6.39-9.91=-53.2 (actual -53.375). \n        # check at 0.5: -36.9-0.71-0.122=-37.73 (actual -37.825). good.\n        if 0.0 < x < 2.0:\n            return -36.9 - 2.842*x*x - 1.958*x**4\n\n        # Region: x >= 2 (large positive growth)\n        # Values: 2->-79.6, 4->-528, 5->-1147.3, 10->-14962.8, 20->-215708.8, 127->-318304442.1\n        # Try -A*exp(k*x). ln(528/79.6)=1.89 over 2 -> k=0.945. \n        # ln(1147.3/528)=0.776 over 1 -> k=0.776. Not constant.\n        # Try -A*exp(k*x^p). \n        # Use 4 and 10: ln(14962.8/528)=3.34 over 6 -> k_eff=0.557\n        # Use 10 and 20: ln(215708.8/14962.8)=2.67 over 10 -> 0.267\n        # Use 20 and 127: ln(318304442/215708.8)=7.30 over 107 -> 0.068\n        # Decelerating in log? Try polynomial in x: \n        # Actually maybe -A*exp(k*x) with k~0.15? at 127: exp(19)=1.8e8 * A. 318M/1.8e8=1.77. \n        # at 20: exp(3)=20.1*1.77=35.6, actual 215708. no.\n        # Try -A*exp(k*x^1.5)? \n        # Let's fit power: ln|y| vs x. \n        # x=4: ln=6.27; x=10: 9.61; x=20: 12.28; x=127: 19.58\n        # Slope between 4&10: 0.556; 10&20: 0.267; 20&127: 0.068\n        # Looks like ln|y| ~ a + b*ln(x)? \n        # x=4: 6.27; x=10: 9.61; slope=(9.61-6.27)/ln(2.5)=3.34/0.916=3.65\n        # x=10 to 127: (19.58-9.61)/ln(12.7)=9.97/2.54=3.92\n        # x=20 to 127: (19.58-12.28)/ln(6.35)=7.30/1.85=3.95\n        # So |y| ~ C * x^3.9? At x=4: C=528/4^3.9=528/224=2.36. \n        # At x=127: 2.36*127^3.9=2.36*127^3.9. 127^3.9=exp(3.9*4.844)=exp(18.89)=1.6e8 -> 3.8e8. Actual 3.18e8. Close!\n        # Try exponent 3.85: 127^3.85=exp(18.65)=1.25e8*2.36=2.95e8. \n        # Try C*x^3.9 with C=2.36: at 20: 2.36*20^3.9=2.36*exp(3.9*3.0)=2.36*exp(11.68)=2.36*1.18e5=2.79e5 (actual 2.16e5). \n        # Try C=2.0, p=3.9: at 4: 2*224=448 (actual 528). \n        # Try fit two points: 4 and 127: C*4^p=528, C*127^p=3.18e8\n        # (127/4)^p = 3.18e8/528 = 6.02e5 -> p*ln(31.75)=13.31 -> p*3.458=13.31 -> p=3.85\n        # C=528/4^3.85=528/exp(3.85*1.386)=528/exp(5.337)=528/207.9=2.54\n        # Check at 10: 2.54*10^3.85=2.54*exp(8.865)=2.54*7080=17983 (actual 14963). \n        # Check at 20: 2.54*20^3.85=2.54*exp(11.54)=2.54*1.03e5=2.62e5 (actual 2.16e5).\n        # Reasonable. Let's use C=2.4, p=3.87.\n        # Check 4: 2.4*4^3.87=2.4*exp(5.365)=2.4*214=514 (actual 528). good.\n        # Check 10: 2.4*10^3.87=2.4*exp(8.91)=2.4*7400=17760 (actual 14963). ~19% high.\n        # Check 20: 2.4*20^3.87=2.4*exp(11.6)=2.4*1.09e5=2.6e5 (actual 2.16e5). ~20% high.\n        # Check 127: 2.4*127^3.87=2.4*exp(18.75)=2.4*1.39e8=3.34e8 (actual 3.18e8). good.\n        # Use p=3.9, C=2.3: 4->2.3*224=515; 10->2.3*7600=17480; 127->2.3*1.6e8=3.68e8. \n        # Fine, approximate.\n        if x >= 2.0:\n            val = -2.4 * (x ** 3.87)\n            if val < FLOOR:\n                return FLOOR\n            return val\n\n        # Region: x <= -2 (large negative growth)\n        # Values: -3->-15, -4->-106.1, -6->-876.9, -10->-8905.7, -20->-167619.7, \n        # -50->-7122681.7, -92->-83623338.1 (then floor)\n        # ln|y|: -3:2.71; -4:4.66; -6:6.78; -10:9.09; -20:12.03; -50:15.78; -92:18.24\n        # Slope: -3 to -10: (9.09-2.71)/7=0.911; -10 to -20: 0.294; -20 to -50: 0.125; -50 to -92: 0.058\n        # Again power law: ln|y| vs ln|x|\n        # |x|=3: 2.71; |x|=4: 4.66; |x|=6: 6.78; |x|=10: 9.09; |x|=20: 12.03; |x|=50: 15.78; |x|=92: 18.24\n        # ln|x|: 1.10, 1.39, 1.79, 2.30, 3.00, 3.91, 4.52\n        # slope 3->10: (9.09-2.71)/(2.30-1.10)=6.38/1.20=5.32\n        # slope 10->20: (12.03-9.09)/(3.00-2.30)=2.94/0.70=4.20\n        # slope 20->50: (15.78-12.03)/(3.91-3.00)=3.75/0.91=4.12\n        # slope 50->92: (18.24-15.78)/(4.52-3.91)=2.46/0.61=4.03\n        # So |y| ~ C*|x|^4.1 for large |x|. \n        # Fit at 20: C*20^4.1=167619.7 -> 20^4.1=exp(4.1*3.0)=exp(12.3)=2.19e5 -> C=0.765\n        # At 50: 0.765*50^4.1=0.765*exp(4.1*3.91)=0.765*exp(16.03)=0.765*9.15e6=7.0e6 (actual 7.12e6). \n        # At 92: 0.765*92^4.1=0.765*exp(4.1*4.52)=0.765*exp(18.53)=0.765*1.12e8=8.57e7 (actual 8.36e7). good.\n        # At 3: 0.765*3^4.1=0.765*exp(4.1*1.10)=0.765*exp(4.51)=0.765*91=69.6 (actual 15). off.\n        # At 4: 0.765*4^4.1=0.765*exp(4.1*1.386)=0.765*exp(5.68)=0.765*293=224 (actual 106). off.\n        # For |x| in [2,6] use the small curve extrapolation instead.\n        # Actually -2 to -6: values -0.1, -15, -106.1, -876.9. \n        # At -2: -0.1 (from small curve). At -3: -15. At -4: -106.1. At -6: -876.9.\n        # Try -A*exp(k*|x|^2)? at 3: -15, at 4: -106 -> ratio 7 over (16-9)=7 -> k=ln7/7=0.278\n        # A*e^(0.278*9)=15 -> A=15/e^2.5=15/12.2=1.23\n        # at 6: 1.23*e^(0.278*36)=1.23*e^10=1.23*22026=27092 (actual 877). no.\n        # Try power law with lower exponent for mid range.\n        # Use interpolation: for |x| in [2,6], fit C*|x|^p.\n        # -3:15, -6:877 -> (6/3)^p=877/15=58.5 -> p*ln2=4.07 -> p=5.87\n        # C=15/3^5.87=15/exp(5.87*1.10)=15/exp(6.45)=15/633=0.0237\n        # check -4: 0.0237*4^5.87=0.0237*exp(5.87*1.386)=0.0237*exp(8.14)=0.0237*3420=81 (actual 106). close.\n        # check -2: 0.0237*2^5.87=0.0237*exp(5.87*0.693)=0.0237*exp(4.07)=0.0237*58.5=1.39 (actual -0.1). off.\n        # Smooth blend: for |x| in [2,6], use C*|x|^5.87 with C=0.0237, but at 2 gives -1.39 vs -0.1.\n        # Let's just use power law p=5.87 for |x|>=3, and for 2<=|x|<3 blend.\n        # Actually the small curve at -2 gives -0.1, at -3 gives -15. Let's just use:\n        # |x| in [2,3]: use -0.1 - 14.9*((|x|-2)/1)^2? at 3: -15. ok.\n        # |x| >= 3: use -0.0237*|x|^5.87 but for large |x| switch to p=4.1.\n        # Hmm, let's check: at 10, p=5.87 gives 0.0237*10^5.87=0.0237*exp(5.87*2.30)=0.0237*exp(13.5)=0.0237*7.3e5=17300 (actual 8906). high.\n        # at 20: 0.0237*20^5.87=0.0237*exp(5.87*3.0)=0.0237*exp(17.6)=0.0237*4.4e7=1.04e6 (actual 1.68e5). way high.\n        # So exponent decreases with |x|. Use p=4.1 for large, but with a different C.\n        # C=0.765, p=4.1 at 10: 0.765*10^4.1=0.765*exp(9.43)=0.765*12500=9560 (actual 8906). good!\n        # at 6: 0.765*6^4.1=0.765*exp(4.1*1.79)=0.765*exp(7.34)=0.765*1540=1178 (actual 877). ok.\n        # at 4: 0.765*4^4.1=224 (actual 106). high.\n        # at 3: 0.765*3^4.1=69.6 (actual 15). high.\n        # So use p=4.1 with C=0.765 for |x|>=6, and interpolate below.\n        # For |x| in [3,6], use p=5.87, C=0.0237.\n        if x <= -2.0:\n            ax = -x\n            if ax < 3.0:\n                # 2 to 3\n                t = ax - 2.0\n                val = -0.1 - 14.9 * t * t\n            elif ax < 6.0:\n                val = -0.0237 * (ax ** 5.87)\n            else:\n                val = -0.765 * (ax ** 4.1)\n            if val < FLOOR:\n                return FLOOR\n            return val\n\n        # Fallback (shouldn't hit)\n        return 0.0\n\n    ys = [f(xv) for xv in probe[\"x\"]]\n    return {\"y\": ys}\n", "notes": "", "since": 24, "theirs": [0.6], "ours": [0.5], "fit": 0.7291666666666666, "size": 917}